      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The primary argument for facial recognition is that it acts as a real-time shield against mass-casualty events, allowing authorities to neutralize threats before they can strike in crowded transit systems. Proponents argue that the cost of a single terrorist attack or a serial killer's rampage far outweighs any theoretical privacy loss, making the technology an essential tool for modern urban survival. Without this capability, cities are left vulnerable to coordinated violence that could result in hundreds of deaths within minutes. Therefore, the safety imperative is viewed by many as an absolute necessity that justifies the intrusion into personal data.",
